const faq = [
  { q: `What charger does my Kindle use?`, a: `It depends on the model year. In Amazon's own user guides, the 2021 Paperwhite, 2022 Kindle, 2024 Paperwhite, 2024 Colorsoft Signature Edition and the Scribe all use a USB-C port, while the 2018 Paperwhite, 2019 Kindle, Oasis and Voyage use micro-USB. For the 2026 lineup, press coverage says the Signature Editions have a USB-C port; we did not find an explicit port statement for the other 2026 models. See the <a href="#ports">port table</a>, and check the port on your own device if you are unsure: micro-USB is tapered, USB-C is a rounded oval that goes in either way up.` },
  { q: `Does a Kindle come with a charger?`, a: `Usually it comes with a cable but not a wall adapter. Amazon's 2024 Paperwhite listing says the box holds the Kindle, a USB-C charging cable and a quick start guide, and its user guides say the Amazon 5W or 9W charger is "sold separately." Amazon's Scribe listings also list a USB-C cable but no adapter. Any USB wall adapter or computer port that meets safety standards can be used, with different charge times, as explained in <a href="#adapters">the adapter section</a>.` },
  { q: `Can I use my phone charger on a Kindle?`, a: `Amazon's user guides say third-party adapters work: they give "less than three hours" for the USB-C Paperwhite, Scribe and Colorsoft, and "less than four hours" for the 2022 Kindle and the micro-USB models, against "less than two hours" with Amazon's own 5W or 9W adapter in the USB-C guides, "but may take longer depending on the capability of the hardware." (The 2019 Kindle and Voyage guides give "less than four hours" even with a Kindle AC adapter.) Amazon also tells owners to use a charger or USB port that complies with safety standards such as IEC 62368. We have not tested any phone charger with a Kindle. Use a reputable, certified adapter and a cable that matches the port.` },
  { q: `Is a higher-wattage charger faster or safer for a Kindle?`, a: `Amazon's own figures stop at modest wattages. Its guides name 5W adapters for most models, 9W for the Colorsoft Signature Edition, and its 2025 Scribe listings name a 20W adapter. For the Scribe Colorsoft, Amazon's compliance page says the charger should deliver between 2.5 and 15 W "to achieve the maximum charging speed," which suggests that more power than that is not expected to speed things up. We found no Amazon statement on USB Power Delivery for Kindles, so we cannot say a bigger adapter charges faster. A fast phone or laptop brick is not something Amazon documents, so choose a reputable one and expect Kindle-level speeds.` },
  { q: `Can I charge a Kindle from my computer?`, a: `Yes, Amazon's guides say you can use the supplied cable to charge from a computer, but it is slower. Amazon's listing for the 2024 Scribe says a full charge takes about 7 hours from a computer against about 2.5 hours with a 9W USB-C adapter. Two cautions from Amazon's guides: a low-powered USB port, such as those on some keyboards and older computers, "will not receive enough power to charge," and a Kindle in USB drive mode cannot be used for reading until you eject it from your computer, after which it keeps charging.` },
  { q: `Why is my Kindle not charging?`, a: `Start with Amazon's own checks: push the cable fully into the Kindle and the adapter or computer, try a different USB port or wall outlet, and look for the lightning bolt in the battery icon and the indicator light turning amber while charging and green when full. If it is connected to a computer, eject it so it leaves USB drive mode. If the Kindle seems frozen, Amazon's guides say to hold the power button until the power dialog appears (the 2024 Paperwhite guide says about 9 seconds) and tap Restart, and if no dialog appears to hold it for 30 seconds or until the LED stops blinking. Some sections of the same guides, and the Scribe guide, say 15 seconds instead. See <a href="#troubleshooting">the troubleshooting section</a> for the full list.` },
  { q: `What charger does the 2026 Kindle, Paperwhite or Colorsoft use?`, a: `Amazon's October 1, 2026 announcement says the Signature Edition Paperwhite and Colorsoft add "pogo pin dock charging," and The Verge says those editions also have a USB-C port and, unlike the 2024 Signature Edition, do not support Qi wireless charging. We did not find Amazon's adapter wattage or charge times for the 2026 models; as of ${FACTS_AS_OF_OCT5} the Paperwhite and Colorsoft were pre-order, shipping October 28, 2026. Re-check the listing for your model when it ships.` },
  { q: `Can I charge a waterproof Kindle if it just got wet?`, a: `Not until it is dry. Amazon's safety information says not to charge the device near water or in extremely humid conditions, and that if it gets wet you should carefully unplug all cables without getting your hands wet and let it dry completely before plugging the cables in again, without using a heat source such as a hair dryer or microwave. A waterproof rating describes immersion, not a damp charging port.` },
